`GetMesg` is still called once. The field scan now reads `numFields` and the `fields` pointer into locals. It walks the array with a plain pointer instead of indexing through `mesg` on every iteration. The function returns the same index, or `FIT_UINT16_INVALID`, in every case.

```cpp
const FIT_UINT16 Profile::GetFieldIndex(const FIT_UINT16 mesgNum, const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    const MESG *mesg = GetMesg(mesgNum);

    if (mesg == NULL)
        return FIT_UINT16_INVALID;

    const FIT_UINT16 count = mesg->numFields;
    const auto *fields = mesg->fields;
    const auto *f = fields;

    for (FIT_UINT16 i = 0; i < count; i++, f++)
    {
        if (f->num == fieldNum)
            return i;
    }

    return FIT_UINT16_INVALID;
}
```